---
import '../../styles/fraunces.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '../../styles/global.css';

const chapters = [
  { id: 'open', t: 0, still: '00', kicker: 'OPEN', title: 'Two distances' },
  { id: 'architect', t: 58, still: '01', kicker: 'ACT 01', title: 'The Architect' },
  { id: 'brasilia', t: 128, still: '02', kicker: 'ACT 02', title: 'Brasília' },
  { id: 'evidence', t: 232, still: '03', kicker: 'ACT 03', title: 'When ambition becomes evidence' },
  { id: 'scales', t: 312, still: '04', kicker: 'ACT 04', title: 'AI scales what is there' },
  { id: 'twins', t: 404, still: '05', kicker: 'ACT 05', title: 'AI digital twins' },
  { id: 'close', t: 504, still: '06', kicker: 'ACT 06', title: 'Close' },
];

const script = [
  {
    id: 'architect',
    t: 58,
    n: '01',
    title: 'The architect',
    paras: [
      'I am an architect. Not as a metaphor. I studied architecture, I drew buildings, and then I spent the last twenty years designing something less visible: data and AI governance.',
      'I work inside a chemical company, like many of you, and I have got plenty of these things wrong myself. But I keep seeing the same problem: we design from above, not always for the person who has to live with the result.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'brasilia',
    t: 128,
    n: '02',
    title: 'Brasília',
    paras: [
      'Let me take you to Brasília. From the air, it is extraordinary: monumental, precise, unforgettable. But at street level, it can feel very different. The scale is vast. The distances are large. A city can make perfect sense from a helicopter and feel completely different when you walk through it.',
      'We build governance in a similar way. We have policies, controls, committees, operating models and, occasionally, a beautiful RACI that makes everyone feel civilisation has finally arrived.',
      'For about ten minutes. Then someone asks who is actually accountable.',
      'Then the framework reaches the plant.',
      'I have been the person with the beautiful drawing. I have presented the framework, watched people nod, and then watched them carry on exactly as before. They were not being difficult. I had built them a plaza nobody wanted to stand in.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'evidence',
    t: 232,
    n: '03',
    title: 'When ambition becomes evidence',
    paras: [
      'That matters when we talk about sustainable digital transformation. We set ambitions, targets and roadmaps. We invest in systems, automation and AI. But eventually, ambition has to become evidence.',
      'A carbon number looks like chemistry. It is a data product.',
      'Behind one apparently simple number sit supplier declarations, energy data, production records, transport data, allocation rules and assumptions. Much of it comes from systems that were never designed to agree with one another.',
      'So the challenge is not simply calculating the number. The challenge is being able to explain it. Where did it come from? Who owns it? What definition sits behind it? And who is prepared to stand behind it when someone asks a difficult question?',
      'You cannot report what you cannot trace.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'scales',
    t: 312,
    n: '04',
    title: 'AI scales what is there',
    paras: [
      'Then, inevitably, someone says: “Why do we not just use AI?”',
      'I am optimistic about AI. But AI does not remove ambiguity. It can scale it.',
      'If five people use the word “batch” to mean five different things, putting an AI agent on top does not make the organisation clearer. It just gives the confusion a faster processor.',
      'Sometimes AI is the answer. Sometimes the answer is better data. Sometimes it is a better process. And occasionally it is simply agreeing on what a word means before we ask a machine to interpret it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'twins',
    t: 404,
    n: '05',
    title: 'Digital twins and trust',
    paras: [
      'And take digital twins. I do not need to define them for this audience. The interesting question is whether anyone believes them.',
      'If equipment data is incomplete, if yield means something different in two systems, or if nobody is accountable for the assumptions, the twin is still only a representation on a screen.',
      'It becomes valuable when the operator trusts it, the engineer understands what sits behind it, and someone is accountable when it is wrong.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'close',
    t: 504,
    n: '06',
    title: 'Close',
    paras: [
      'So I want to leave you with one question.',
      'What is one word in your organisation that means something different depending on which floor you are standing on?',
      'Ask it at lunch. You may discover that the answer tells you more about your governance than another hundred pages of framework ever could.',
      'Agents do not own risk. They do not carry accountability.',
      'Humans do. Always.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Data and AI in Sustainable Digital Transformation · EDUARDO sopalda</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="door">
      <a class="door-mark" href="/"><span>EDUARDO</span> sopalda</a>
      <a class="door-stop" href="/out-loud">Out Loud</a>
      <nav class="door-nav" aria-label="This talk">
        <a href="#film">Film</a>
        <a href="#script">Script</a>
        <a href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a>
      </nav>
      <a class="door-back" href="/">Back to the field</a>
    </header>
    <div class="nerve" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="desk">
      <header class="mast">
        <div>
          <h1>Data and AI in Sustainable Digital Transformation</h1>
          <p class="deck">From Brasília to the Plant Floor</p>
          <p class="event">AUTOMA Chem 2026 · Estrel Berlin · 26 October · 9:40</p>
          <div class="downloads" id="roadmap">
            <a href="/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/roadmap.pdf" download="AUTOMA-Chem-2026-Roadmap.pdf">Download the roadmap (PDF)</a>
            <a href="/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/film.mp4" download="AUTOMA-Chem-2026-Eduardo-Sopalda-10min.mp4">Download the film (MP4)</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="who"><strong>Eduardo Sopalda</strong><span>D&T · Global Data Governance Lead</span></p>
      </header>

      <div class="desk-body">
        <section class="stage" id="film" aria-label="Film">
          <div class="frame">
            <video
              id="talk-film"
              src="/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/film.mp4"
              poster="/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/00.jpg"
              playsinline
              muted
              preload="metadata"
            ></video>
          </div>
          <div class="transport">
            <button class="pp" id="talk-play" type="button" aria-label="Play">Play</button>
            <input class="scrub" id="talk-scrub" type="range" min="0" max="600" step="0.1" value="0" aria-label="Film position" />
            <div class="times" id="talk-time">0:00 / 10:00</div>
          </div>
          <div class="strip" id="talk-strip">
            {
              chapters.map((c) => (
                <button type="button" data-t={c.t} data-id={c.id} data-kicker={c.kicker} data-title={c.title} aria-label={c.title}>
                  <img src={`/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/${c.still}.jpg`} alt="" />
                </button>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </section>
        <aside class="rail" aria-label="Acts">
          <div class="act-kicker" id="talk-kicker">OPEN</div>
          <h2 class="act-title" id="talk-act">Two distances</h2>
          <div class="copper-rule"></div>
          <p class="line" id="talk-line">Data and AI in sustainable digital transformation. From Brasília to the plant floor.</p>
          <ol class="chapters">
            {
              chapters.map((c, i) => (
                <li>
                  <button type="button" data-t={c.t} data-id={c.id} data-kicker={c.kicker} data-title={c.title}>
                    <small>{String(i).padStart(2, '0')}</small>
                    <strong>{c.title}</strong>
                  </button>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ol>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <section class="script" id="script" aria-label="Speaking script">
        <div class="script-head">
          <h2>Speaking script</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="script-body">
          {
            script.map((s) => (
              <article id={`act-${s.id}`} data-id={s.id}>
                <button type="button" data-t={s.t} data-id={s.id}>
                  <small>{s.n}</small>
                  <span>{s.title}</span>
                </button>
                {s.paras.map((para) => (
                  <p>{para}</p>
                ))}
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var video = document.getElementById('talk-film');
        var play = document.getElementById('talk-play');
        var scrub = document.getElementById('talk-scrub');
        var timeEl = document.getElementById('talk-time');
        var kicker = document.getElementById('talk-kicker');
        var act = document.getElementById('talk-act');
        var line = document.getElementById('talk-line');
        var buttons = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-t]'));
        var chapters = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.chapters [data-t]'));
        // Cached once -- mark() (below) used to re-run both of these on
        // every single 'timeupdate' tick (many times a second during
        // playback) for a DOM that never changes after load. Audit
        // finding; no visual behavior changes, same elements either way.
        var scriptArticles = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.script-body article'));
        var stripButtons = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.strip [data-t]'));
        var cues = [
          [0, 'Data and AI in sustainable digital transformation. From Brasília to the plant floor.'],
          [58, '…not as a metaphor.'],
          [112, 'We design from above. Not always for the person who has to live with the result.'],
          [128, 'From above, every line found its place.'],
          [168, 'Below, every line met a person.'],
          [210, 'I built a plaza nobody wanted to stand in.'],
          [240, '11,001.8 kt CO₂e. It is a data product.'],
          [276, 'The number is ours. Much of the evidence is elsewhere.'],
          [312, 'AI scales what is there.'],
          [372, 'Sometimes AI is the answer. Sometimes the answer is better data. Sometimes it is a better process.'],
          [404, 'AI digital twins and smarter decisions.'],
          [468, 'Helping people find better ways to run the systems they already have, with less waste built in.'],
          [504, 'Agents do not own risk. They do not carry accountability. Humans do. Always.'],
          [540, 'Agents do not own risk. They do not carry accountability.'],
          [572, 'Humans do. Always.']
        ];
        if (!video || !play || !scrub) return;

        function fmt(s) {
          if (!isFinite(s) || s < 0) s = 0;
          var m = Math.floor(s / 60);
          var r = Math.floor(s % 60);
          return m + ':' + String(r).padStart(2, '0');
        }

        function mark(t) {
          var current = chapters[0];
          chapters.forEach(function (b) {
            if (Number(b.getAttribute('data-t')) <= t + 0.15) current = b;
          });
          if (!current) return;
          var id = current.getAttribute('data-id');
          chapters.forEach(function (b) {
            b.classList.toggle('on', b === current);
          });
          scriptArticles.forEach(function (article) {
            article.classList.toggle('on', article.getAttribute('data-id') === id);
          });
          if (kicker) kicker.textContent = current.getAttribute('data-kicker') || '';
          if (act) act.textContent = current.getAttribute('data-title') || '';
          var spoken = cues[0][1];
          cues.forEach(function (c) {
            if (c[0] <= t + 0.15) spoken = c[1];
          });
          if (line) line.textContent = spoken;
          stripButtons.forEach(function (b) {
            var on = b.getAttribute('data-id') === id;
            b.classList.toggle('on', on);
            if (on) b.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
            else b.removeAttribute('aria-current');
          });
        }

        function paint() {
          var d = video.duration || 600;
          scrub.max = String(d);
          scrub.value = String(video.currentTime || 0);
          scrub.style.setProperty('--p', (video.currentTime / d) * 100 + '%');
          if (timeEl) timeEl.textContent = fmt(video.currentTime) + ' / ' + fmt(d);
          mark(video.currentTime || 0);
          play.textContent = video.paused ? 'Play' : 'Pause';
          play.setAttribute('aria-label', video.paused ? 'Play' : 'Pause');
        }

        function go(t) {
          video.currentTime = t;
          var pending = video.play();
          if (pending && pending.catch) pending.catch(function () {});
        }

        play.addEventListener('click', function () {
          if (video.paused) {
            var pending = video.play();
            if (pending && pending.catch) pending.catch(function () {});
          } else video.pause();
        });
        scrub.addEventListener('input', function () {
          video.currentTime = Number(scrub.value);
          paint();
        });
        buttons.forEach(function (b) {
          if (b === scrub) return;
          b.addEventListener('click', function () {
            go(Number(b.getAttribute('data-t')));
          });
        });
        video.addEventListener('timeupdate', paint);
        video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', paint);
        video.addEventListener('play', paint);
        video.addEventListener('pause', paint);
        document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
          var tag = e.target && e.target.tagName;
          if (tag === 'INPUT' || tag === 'TEXTAREA') return;
          if (e.key === ' ' || e.key === 'k') {
            e.preventDefault();
            play.click();
          }
        });
        // Audit finding: this used to autoplay the full 10-minute film
        // the instant the page loaded (muted, so browsers allowed it,
        // but nobody asked for 10 minutes of video to start downloading
        // on page load, mobile data included). Starts paused on its
        // poster frame instead -- play(), the chapter strip/rail, and
        // the script-body jump buttons (go(), above) are all still the
        // real way to start it, untouched.
        mark(0);
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  html {
    overflow-y: auto;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    background: #e9d4ba;
  }

  body {
    overflow-x: hidden;
    overflow-y: auto;
    margin: 0;
    background: #e9d4ba;
    color: #0f0f11;
  }

  .door {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem 0.7rem;
    background: #000;
    color: #f3ebe0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .door a {
    color: #f3ebe0;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .door-mark {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  }

  .door-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.15rem;
  }

  .door-back {
    justify-self: end;
  }

  .door a:hover,
  .door a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .door a:focus-visible,
  button:focus-visible {
    outline: 1.5px solid var(--gold);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .nerve {
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.55) 12%, rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.55) 88%, transparent);
  }

  .desk {
    background: #e9d4ba;
    color: #0f0f11;
  }

  .mast {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-end;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #c4a888;
  }

  h1,
  .deck,
  .act-title,
  .script-head h2,
  .script-body button {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .mast h1 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 18ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.4vw, 2.15rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .deck {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem);
  }

  .event,
  .who,
  .downloads a,
  .times,
  .act-kicker,
  .chapters button,
  .hint {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .event {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #365f7c;
  }

  .downloads {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
  }

  .downloads a {
    color: #762f0b;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #762f0b;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .who {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: right;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .who strong,
  .who span {
    display: block;
  }

  .who span {
    color: #48565f;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  .desk-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(240px, 320px);
  }

  .stage {
    border-right: 1px solid #c4a888;
  }

  .frame video {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: calc(100dvh - 9.5rem);
    background: #dcc4a6;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .transport {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem 0.9rem;
  }

  .pp {
    min-width: 4.5rem;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid #762f0b;
    background: transparent;
    color: #762f0b;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  .times {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #48565f;
  }

  .strip {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 0 1rem 0.85rem;
  }

  .strip button {
    flex: 0 0 8.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .strip img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .strip button.on {
    border-bottom-color: #762f0b;
  }

  .line {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    min-height: 4.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .scrub {
    width: 100%;
    accent-color: #762f0b;
  }

  .rail {
    padding: 1.1rem;
  }

  .act-kicker {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: #365f7c;
  }

  .act-title {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.65rem;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .copper-rule {
    height: 2px;
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0.9rem;
    background: #762f0b;
  }

  .chapters {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .chapters button,
  .script-body button {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .chapters button {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.4rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.4rem;
    border-left: 2px solid transparent;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .chapters button.on,
  .script-body article.on {
    border-left-color: #762f0b;
    background: rgba(220, 196, 166, 0.55);
  }

  .chapters small,
  .script-body small {
    color: #365f7c;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  .script {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 260px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid #c4a888;
  }

  .script-head {
    padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem 1.6rem;
  }

  .script-head h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
  }

  .script-body {
    border-left: 1px solid #c4a888;
  }

  .script-body article {
    padding: 1rem 1.6rem 1.15rem 1.15rem;
    border-left: 2px solid transparent;
  }

  .script-body button {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.6rem 1fr;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .script-body p {
    margin: 0.55rem 0 0 2.95rem;
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .door {
      grid-template-columns: auto auto 1fr auto;
      align-items: center;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .mast,
    .desk-body,
    .script {
      display: block;
    }

    .who {
      text-align: left;
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
    }

    .stage {
      border-right: 0;
    }

    .script-body {
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid #c4a888;
    }

    .script-body p {
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
